BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsilentfilmseries3awings192726106-20261128@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261127T192538Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
SUMMARY:SILENT FILM Series: Wings (1927)
DESCRIPTION:Soar into the spectacle and emotion of Wings \, the first film to ever win the Academy Award for Best Picture. Set against the backdrop of World War I\, this drama follows two young fighter pilots whose rivalry\, friendship\, and love for the same woman unfold amid the danger and excitement of aerial combat. Featuring astonishing flight photography and large-scale action sequences that still inspire and awe nearly a century later\, Wings combines thrilling adventure with heartfelt human drama. STARS: Clara Bowm Richard Arlen\, Charles Rogers\, Gary Cooper RUNTIME: 114 Minutes GENRE: Silent\, Action\, Drama\, Romance\, War RATING: PG-13 This show is part of the Silent Film Series\, celebrating timeless scores and classic films. When the lights go down and the Mighty Wurlitzer rises from the orchestra pit\, audiences are treated to a live organ performance featuring Tedde Gibson—complete with a short musical set before the credits roll and a brief introduction to each silent film. Our beloved Wurlitzer turns 100 this December\, having filled the theater with music for nearly a century. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop for a unique film experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/silent-film-series%3a-wings-(1927)/26106/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
